WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.310
Things are not looking good for Luc Besson's
sci-fi epic Valerian and the City of a Thousand

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:05.810
Planets.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:10.820
The expensive film was obliterated at the
domestic box office in its opening weekend,

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:17.040
falling in fifth place with only $17 million
against a reported $180 million production

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:17.540
budget.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:22.180
Considering the weight Besson's name carries
with sci-fi fans, many may be surprised to

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:25.760
hear that his most recent outing had that
much trouble finding an audience.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:30.140
However, there were actually quite a few warning
signs that Valerian would fail.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:34.840
Here are the real reasons why Valerian was
an intergalactic disappointment at the box

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:35.400
office.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:37.700
Little-known source material

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.110
Valerian is based on the French comic strip
which ran from 1967 to 2010.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.480
Besson had been reading the comic since he
was a child, and dreamed of adapting it into

00:00:47.489 --> 00:00:48.680
a film for years.

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:52.290
But he had to wait until he had the right
technology and experience to pull off the

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:53.560
comic's unique vision.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:58.440
Despite its wide readership overseas, though,
the comic never quite found an audience in

00:00:58.449 --> 00:00:59.469
the United States.

00:00:59.469 --> 00:01:04.630
So, when the title for Besson's passion project
popped up on potential audiences' feeds, a

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:08.750
lot of people weren't as familiar with the
comic characters as some of those other superhero

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:11.080
stories that tend to tear up the box office.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:15.360
The familiarity factor that's such a draw
for similar adventure movies was gone right

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:16.260
from the start.

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:18.100
Story confusion

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:23.130
Compounding the confusion was the fact that
Valerian seemed to offer audiences vague marketing

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:27.420
materials that didn't little to explain what
Valerian was actually about.

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:32.580
The previews focused heavily on the film's
style over its content and focused on off-putting

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:33.800
aspects of the story.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:36.020
"You flirt.

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:37.000
I smile."

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:42.070
None of the trailers took the time to go through
the reality of the threat against Alpha or

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:46.600
to discuss why Valerian and Laureline were
chosen to stop it, which made the previews

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:48.520
feel hollow and unimpressionable.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:53.200
"We need the two of you to be the guardians
of our future."

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:57.120
While the marketing might've drawn in a few
viewers who'd want to see Besson's visual

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:01.850
spectacle unfold, focusing entirely on the
style over substance in the marketing wasn't

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:03.380
necessarily a smart choice.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:08.060
Since a lot of would-be audience members aren't
familiar with the comic series, that lack

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:11.180
of understanding may have just been a turn-off
at the ticket booth.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:13.020
Ho-hum reviews

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:17.680
Some well-established sci-fi worlds have been
able to pull in both dedicated and casual

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:22.190
fans alike, while others have struggled to
find the mass market appeal necessary to make

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:23.320
up their huge budgets.

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:28.280
As with any movie with an unusual premise,
good reviews can be a huge boost to creating

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:31.880
audience interest when there's not already-established
fan-base in place.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:35.660
With Valerian, though, the critical love line
wasn't quite there.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:40.100
Some reviews panned the leads for not having
chemistry and called the story empty, with

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:44.540
the impressive visuals being singled out as
a lone point of positivity for the film.

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:48.780
Those middling reviews were hardly enough
to bring in sci-fi skeptics who'd maybe been

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:50.580
on the fence about seeing the movie.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:52.140
Up-and-coming actors

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:57.340
Although Dane DeHaan and Cara Delevingne are
both well known amidst industry circles, neither

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:01.069
have established themselves as bankable blockbuster
stars just yet.

00:03:01.069 --> 00:03:05.990
DeHaan is best known for his indie film appearances,
while Delevingne only recently made the switch

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:08.220
from modeling into the movie star business.

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:13.080
Even those popcorn flicks they have appeared
in -- The Amazing Spider-Man 2 and Suicide

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:17.500
Squad, respectively -- were largely disappointments
and did nothing to prove their profitability

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:19.820
or earn them household name recognition.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:21.220
Stiff competition

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:25.660
The opening weekend for Valerian was packed
with alternative options for the theater-going

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:29.940
crowd, including Christopher Nolan's widely
praised war epic Dunkirk.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:35.400
The film offered the visual dynamism Valerian
promised, and it had gripping true story subject

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:36.500
matter at the center.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:41.420
Meanwhile, the R-rated ensemble comedy Girls'
Trip offered viewers a chance to let loose

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:45.770
and enjoy some adult humor, which may have
been a draw-in for those that are experiencing

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:47.520
a bit of superhero summer fatigue.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:52.420
The film also came out just two weeks after
Marvel's juggernaut Spider-Man: Homecoming

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:56.170
and just one week after the trilogy-ender
War for the Planet of the Apes.

00:03:56.170 --> 00:04:01.190
While both films saw their box office performances
pushed beyond initial expectations due to

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:05.780
strong reviews, it was easy to see that they'd
have legs long past their release dates.

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:10.400
The combined array of those four other options
might have given theatergoers some pause about

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.180
choosing to see Valerian, too.

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:13.640
Creative salvation?

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:18.040
A number of different figures have been thrown
around for Valerian's budget, but they all

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:20.389
point to one thing — it was high.

00:04:20.389 --> 00:04:24.960
The film, which has been reported as the most
expensive French production of all time, likely

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:28.600
cost somewhere around $200 million including
marketing.

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:31.160
"Yeah, well, time flies when you're having
fun."

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:35.800
That means it'll require a pretty stellar
comeback in order to make a profit.

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:37.420
However, there is still some hope for Valerian.

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:42.380
Like many domestic flops in the summer of
2017, the international box office could be

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:42.880
a savior.

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:47.220
The movie is expected to do big business in
France, where viewers are familiar with the

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:51.440
comics, and will continue to be rolled out
in international territories throughout the

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:51.940
summer.

00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:55.900
The best hope for the film, however, comes
from Besson's creative method of financing

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:56.400
it.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:05:00.840
Tax credits are one of the film's first helpers,
with estimates saying that they bump the film's

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:02.640
cost down by $50 million.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:07.880
The movie is also said to be covering significant
parts of its budget through equity financing

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:08.880
and foreign pre-sales.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:13.440
Still, the slow start for Valerian is not
a good sign for the film in the long run,

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:17.540
and is an even worse sign for Besson's already
planned follow-up films.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:22.440
The movie will have to do significant business
overseas in order to be considered a success,

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:26.960
and it seems unlikely that it will be able
to break its perception as a box office flop.

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:28.260
"HEY."

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:29.560
Thanks for watching!

